[{ "action": "append", "id": "event-modals", "value" : "<div tabindex=\"-1\" id=\"modal-e0b3cc1a-4674-4243-9c7b-8acb0e040dab\" class=\"modal\"><div class=\"modal-dialog modal-lg\"><div class=\"modal-content\"><div class=\"modal-header\"><a data-dismiss=\"modal\" class=\"close\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-remove\"></span></a><p class=\"text-muted\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-road\"></span> Research Papers</p><strong>Thu 15 Oct 2026 17:15 - 17:30 at <a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/room/ase-2026/ase-2026-venue1-forum-8\" class=\"room-link navigate\">Forum 8</a></strong> - <a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/track/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track#program\" class=\"navigate\">Testing and Analysis: Regression and Model-Based Testing 6</a> <small>Chair(s): <a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/ase-2026/andreastocco\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\">Andrea Stocco</a></small></div><div class=\"modal-body\"><div class=\"bg-primary event-title\"><h4><span data-event-star=\"e0b3cc1a-4674-4243-9c7b-8acb0e040dab\" title=\"Add event to your program\"><span class=\"text-disabled glyphicon glyphicon-star-empty\"></span></span><strong>TrackTest: Trajectory Generation and Prioritization for Testing Multiple Object Tracking System</strong></h4></div><div class=\"bg-info event-description\"><p>Multiple Object Tracking (MOT) is a fundamental component of the perception stack in Autonomous Driving Systems (ADS), providing essential state estimation for downstream decision-making. Despite the adoption of multi-sensor fusion to enhance reliability, MOT systems remain susceptible to tracking failures, which can lead to catastrophic safety incidents. Current perception testing and evaluation predominantly rely on manually annotated real-world datasets, which are behaviorally imbalanced, prohibitively expensive to scale, and insufficient to cover diverse dynamic interactions.</p>\n<p>To bridge this gap, we propose TrackTest, an automated testing framework designed to systematically expose tracking failures in MOT systems. TrackTest transforms real-world seed scenarios into challenging test cases by synthesizing physically feasible and behaviorally diverse trajectories. We formulate six representative driving patterns as constraint-based optimization problems for behavior-controllable trajectory generation. To reduce computational overhead, we introduce a trajectory prioritization strategy that identifies high-risk scenarios most likely to trigger tracking failures. We evaluate TrackTest on \\reviseline{six} state-of-the-art MOT systems. Experimental results show that TrackTest effectively generate behavior-diverse trajectories and uncover diverse tracking failures.</p>\n<p></p><a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1145/3832783.3837540\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"publication-link navigate\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-link\"></span> DOI</a><p></p><div class=\"row\"><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/ase-2026/xinyugao\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"micro-avatar\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getDefaultImage/micro-avatar?1783985080000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Xinyu Gao<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">Nanjing University</span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><small>China</small></h5></div></div></a></div><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/ase-2026/haoxinchen\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"micro-avatar\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getDefaultImage/micro-avatar?1783985080000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Haoxin Chen<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">Nanjing University</span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><small>China</small></h5></div></div></a></div></div><div class=\"row\"><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/ase-2026/shuoxiaozhang\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"Shuoxiao Zhang\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getProfileImage/shuoxiaozhang/846313bf-eda7-495a-9843-de12957228c6/micro-avatar?1793538914000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Shuoxiao Zhang<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">Nanjing University</span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><small>China</small></h5></div></div></a></div><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/ase-2026/enyitang1\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"micro-avatar\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getDefaultImage/micro-avatar?1783985080000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Enyi Tang<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">Nanjing University</span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><small>China</small></h5></div></div></a></div></div><div class=\"row\"><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/ase-2026/hengruixu\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"micro-avatar\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getDefaultImage/micro-avatar?1783985080000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Hengrui Xu<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h